searchData={"items":[{"type":"module","title":"MedEx.Capture","doc":"GenServer that writes indexed mono 48 kHz PCM16LE audio to an immutable,\ncontent-addressed WAV file and fans full frames out to a bounded live Opus\npreview branch.","ref":"MedEx.Capture.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Lifecycle & Ownership - MedEx.Capture","doc":"The host starts each capture under its own `DynamicSupervisor` (this module\nuses `restart: :temporary` and registers no global names). Capture monitors\nthe `:owner` producer process and stops, removing its temporary `.part` file,\nif `:owner` exits before `finish/1` succeeds. Only this PID may call\n`push/3` and `finish/1`. Other callers receive `{:error, :not_owner}`.","ref":"MedEx.Capture.html#module-lifecycle-ownership"},{"type":"module","title":"Preview Messages - MedEx.Capture","doc":"A preview peer owner calls `subscribe/1` (single active subscriber; a newer\nsubscriber replaces the previous one) and receives:\n\n  * `{:med_ex_preview, capture_pid, sample_index, opus_payload}` — one\n    encoded 20 ms Opus packet. After sending it with `MedEx.Preview.send_opus/4`,\n    call `demand/1` to request the next packet.\n  * `{:med_ex_preview_replaced, capture_pid}` — sent to the displaced listener\n    when a different process subscribes.\n  * `{:med_ex_preview_failed, capture_pid, reason}` — sent if the internal\n    Opus encoder exits. Capture itself continues uninterrupted and a new\n    subscriber can re-subscribe.","ref":"MedEx.Capture.html#module-preview-messages"},{"type":"function","title":"MedEx.Capture.child_spec/1","doc":"Returns a specification to start this module under a supervisor.\n\nSee `Supervisor`.","ref":"MedEx.Capture.html#child_spec/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedEx.Capture.demand/1","doc":"Signals readiness for the next `{:med_ex_preview, ...}` packet from the\nactive preview subscriber.","ref":"MedEx.Capture.html#demand/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedEx.Capture.finish/1","doc":"Flushes and fsyncs the WAV header, installs the content-addressed\n` .wav` file, fsyncs `:artifact_dir`, and stops the capture.\n\nReturns `{:ok, %MedEx.Evidence{}}`, `{:error, :empty_capture}` if no samples\nwere pushed, `{:error, :artifact_conflict}` if a conflicting file already\nexists at the target digest path, or `{:error, reason}` on filesystem failure.","ref":"MedEx.Capture.html#finish/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedEx.Capture.push/3","doc":"Appends one contiguous mono 48 kHz PCM16LE chunk at `first_sample`.\n\nChunks must start at sample `0`, advance contiguously without gaps, contain\nan even number of bytes in `2..1920` (up to 960 samples / 20 ms), stay within\nthe 30-minute maximum (`86_400_000` samples), and send at most one short tail\nframe (`< 1920` bytes) immediately before `finish/1`.\n\nA non-owner receives `{:error, :not_owner}` and recording continues.\nFor the producer, returns `:ok`, or `{:error, :invalid_frame | File.posix()}` (stopping the\ncapture process and discarding the temporary file).","ref":"MedEx.Capture.html#push/3"},{"type":"function","title":"MedEx.Capture.start_link/1","doc":"Starts a capture process linked to the caller (typically a host `DynamicSupervisor`).","ref":"MedEx.Capture.html#start_link/1"},{"type":"function","title":"Required options - MedEx.Capture.start_link/1","doc":"* `:owner` — PID of the single PCM producer process. Capture monitors this\n    PID and aborts if it exits before `finish/1`.\n  * `:acquisition_id` — host-assigned string identifying this acquisition.\n  * `:artifact_dir` — existing directory where the temporary `.part` file and\n    final ` .wav` artifact are written.","ref":"MedEx.Capture.html#start_link/1-required-options"},{"type":"function","title":"MedEx.Capture.subscribe/1","doc":"Subscribes the calling process to bounded live Opus preview frames.\n\nOnly one preview subscriber is active at a time; subscribing from a new\nprocess replaces the previous subscriber. Returns `:ok` or\n`{:error, :preview_unavailable}`.","ref":"MedEx.Capture.html#subscribe/1"},{"type":"module","title":"MedEx.Evidence","doc":"Finalized evidence returned by `MedEx.Capture.finish/1` for a continuous mono\n48 kHz PCM16LE WAV acquisition.","ref":"MedEx.Evidence.html"},{"type":"module","title":"Fields - MedEx.Evidence","doc":"* `:acquisition_id` — host-supplied acquisition correlation identifier.\n  * `:artifact_key` — content-addressed filename (`\" .wav\"`).\n  * `:file_sha256` — lowercase hex SHA-256 of the complete finalized WAV file.\n  * `:pcm_sha256` — lowercase hex SHA-256 of the raw PCM16LE payload bytes.\n  * `:kind` — modality discriminator (`:audio_pcm16_wav`).\n  * `:sample_rate_hz` — audio sample rate in Hz (`48_000`).\n  * `:first_sample` — inclusive starting sample index (`0`).\n  * `:end_sample` — exclusive ending sample index.\n  * `:sample_count` — total captured mono samples.\n  * `:continuity` — observed source continuity verdict (`:observed_continuous`).","ref":"MedEx.Evidence.html#module-fields"},{"type":"type","title":"MedEx.Evidence.t/0","doc":"","ref":"MedEx.Evidence.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"module","title":"MedEx.Preview","doc":"One replaceable, send-only WebRTC peer for an Opus preview. The caller owns\nthe peer and receives its ExWebRTC state changes. Capture has its own lifetime.","ref":"MedEx.Preview.html"},{"type":"type","title":"MedEx.Preview.t/0","doc":"","ref":"MedEx.Preview.html#t:t/0"},{"type":"function","title":"MedEx.Preview.answer/2","doc":"Answers a receive-only browser audio offer containing the browser's ICE candidates.\n\nThe calling process owns the resulting `ExWebRTC.PeerConnection` and receives\n`{:ex_webrtc, peer.pid, {:connection_state_change, state}}` messages (such as\n`:connected`, `:failed`, and `:closed`). Call `close/1` on teardown.","ref":"MedEx.Preview.html#answer/2"},{"type":"function","title":"Options - MedEx.Preview.answer/2","doc":"* `:ice_servers` — list of ICE server maps passed to `ExWebRTC.PeerConnection`\n    (defaults to `[]` for direct local candidates).\n  * `:ice_transport_policy` — `:all` (default) or `:relay`. For relay-only\n    preview, supply TURN credentials and select relay on the browser too.","ref":"MedEx.Preview.html#answer/2-options"},{"type":"function","title":"MedEx.Preview.close/1","doc":"Stops the underlying WebRTC peer connection if it is still alive.","ref":"MedEx.Preview.html#close/1"},{"type":"function","title":"MedEx.Preview.send_opus/4","doc":"Sends one Opus RTP packet with separate per-peer `sequence` (wrapped mod\n`65_536`) and 48 kHz media clock `sample_index` (wrapped mod `2^32`).","ref":"MedEx.Preview.html#send_opus/4"},{"type":"module","title":"MedEx.Web","doc":"Locates MedEx's packaged browser JavaScript assets.\n\nHost web applications serve these files as `application/javascript` under\ntheir own routes:\n\n  * `\"session_hook.js\"` — LiveView hook helper (`createMedExHook/1`) for the\n    clinician's receive-only WebRTC preview peer.\n  * `\"pcm_capture.js\"` — patient-browser capture helper (`startPCM` with optional input and settings callback) for\n    48 kHz mono PCM16LE microphone capture over an authenticated WebSocket.\n  * `\"pcm_worklet.js\"` — `AudioWorkletProcessor` (`\"med-ex-indexed-pcm\"`)\n    loaded by `startPCM`.","ref":"MedEx.Web.html"},{"type":"function","title":"MedEx.Web.asset_path/1","doc":"Returns the absolute filesystem path to a packaged browser asset.\n\nAccepts `\"session_hook.js\"`, `\"pcm_capture.js\"`, or `\"pcm_worklet.js\"`.","ref":"MedEx.Web.html#asset_path/1"},{"type":"extras","title":"Overview","doc":"# MedEx\n\nMedEx is an Elixir SDK for recording clinical audio and streaming an independent\nlive WebRTC Opus preview. It accepts indexed mono 48 kHz signed PCM16LE audio,\nwrites an immutable content-addressed WAV artifact, and encodes live Opus for a\nreplaceable WebRTC listener. The host application owns authorization, signaling,\nand clinical review.","ref":"readme.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Installation - Overview","doc":"The source tree targets 0.2.0. For a released 0.2.x package, declare the dependency in `mix.exs`.\n\n```elixir\ndef deps do\n  [\n    {:med_ex, \"~> 0.2.0\"}\n  ]\nend\n```","ref":"readme.html#installation"},{"type":"extras","title":"Prerequisites - Overview","doc":"- Elixir `~> 1.20` (tested on Elixir `1.20.5` / OTP `29.1.2`).\n- On Ubuntu 26.04, native WebRTC dependencies (`ex_dtls`, `ex_libsrtp`) require a\n  C compiler, `make`, `pkg-config`, and OpenSSL development headers\n  (`build-essential pkg-config libssl-dev`).\n- Live Opus encoding uses `membrane_opus_plugin`, which downloads precompiled\n  `libopus` binaries on supported Linux/macOS targets and falls back to system\n  `libopus-dev` (`pkg-config`) when building from source.","ref":"readme.html#prerequisites"},{"type":"extras","title":"Quick example - Overview","doc":"```elixir\n# Start a capture under your host DynamicSupervisor (owner is the producer PID)\n{:ok, capture} =\n  DynamicSupervisor.start_child(\n    MyApp.Captures,\n    {MedEx.Capture, owner: self(), acquisition_id: \"acq-1\", artifact_dir: \"/var/lib/myapp/wavs\"}\n  )\n\n# Push contiguous 20 ms chunks (960 mono samples = 1,920 PCM16LE bytes at 48 kHz)\n:ok = MedEx.Capture.push(capture, 0, pcm_chunk_0)\n:ok = MedEx.Capture.push(capture, 960, pcm_chunk_1)\n\n# Finalize to an immutable \" .wav\" file and %MedEx.Evidence{}\n{:ok, %MedEx.Evidence{artifact_key: key, file_sha256: sha, sample_count: 1920}} =\n  MedEx.Capture.finish(capture)\n```","ref":"readme.html#quick-example"},{"type":"extras","title":"Capture and preview in 0.2.0 - Overview","doc":"Only the configured producer PID can push samples or finish the recording.\nThe host can reserve an acquisition ID and directory before opening the microphone\nand recover a finalized file under that ID. One listener at a time receives Opus.\nReplacing it sends the previous subscriber `{:med_ex_preview_replaced, capture}`.\n\nThe browser's `startPCM` takes an optional fifth argument with `deviceId` and\n`onSource`. It reports the diagnostic track's actual settings before recording,\nso the host can select a separate conversation microphone. The PCM transport\nbudget is 250 ms of writer acknowledgement delay plus 50 ms of jitter. The\nclient reports its peak buffered wire bytes and maximum observed WebSocket\nacknowledgement delay. WebRTC preview supports host-provided TURN servers and\nrelay-only ICE policy.","ref":"readme.html#capture-and-preview-in-0-2-0"},{"type":"extras","title":"Guides - Overview","doc":"- [Host integration](guides/host_integration.md) — Elixir capture/preview\n  supervision, Phoenix signaling channel, binary PCM WebSocket contract, and\n  browser hook / AudioWorklet setup.\n- [Architecture and roadmap](guides/architecture_and_roadmap.md) — Capture vs.\n  preview failure domains, shipped vs. planned capabilities, and future\n  integrations.\n- [Source development](guides/source_development.md) — Working in the source\n  monorepo checkout and preparing Weld release bundles.","ref":"readme.html#guides"},{"type":"extras","title":"License - Overview","doc":"Released under the MIT License.","ref":"readme.html#license"},{"type":"extras","title":"Architecture and roadmap","doc":"# Architecture and roadmap\n\nMedEx provides real-time clinical media capture and WebRTC preview transport for\nElixir applications. Host applications own authorization, encounter state,\nclinician review, persistence, and healthcare record export—MedEx has no\ndatabase, Phoenix server, or FHIR dependency.","ref":"architecture_and_roadmap.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Why two separate media paths? - Architecture and roadmap","doc":"Clinical diagnostic audio (such as remote auscultation) has conflicting\nrequirements:\n\n- **Live listening** needs low-latency, resilient WebRTC Opus streaming that can\n  drop packets or reconnect peers across network hiccups.\n- **Authoritative recording** needs bit-exact, continuous, lossless PCM audio\n  whose integrity is never compromised by WebRTC jitter, Opus compression, or\n  clinician browser disconnects.\n\nMedEx enforces this split in its process boundaries: live indexed PCM enters\n`MedEx.Capture`, which writes the lossless WAV directly and fans full 20 ms\nframes out to a bounded, disposable preview branch (`Membrane.Opus.Encoder`\nkept private behind `MedEx.Capture` → `MedEx.Preview` over `ExWebRTC`).\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart LR\n  PCM[\"Indexed PCM16LE (48 kHz)\"] --> Capture[\"MedEx.Capture (Lossless Writer)\"]\n  Capture --> WAV[\"Immutable &lt;sha256&gt;.wav + MedEx.Evidence\"]\n  Capture -. \"bounded 1-frame demand\" .-> Encoder[\"Private Membrane Opus Encoder\"]\n  Encoder --> Peer[\"MedEx.Preview (ExWebRTC)\"]\n  Peer --> Listener[\"Clinician Browser (Replaceable)\"]\n```","ref":"architecture_and_roadmap.html#why-two-separate-media-paths"},{"type":"extras","title":"Process ownership and failure domains - Architecture and roadmap","doc":"| Component | Owner | Failure behavior |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `MedEx.Capture` | Host `DynamicSupervisor` (`restart: :temporary`, no global names) | Accepts writes and finish from its monitored `:owner` PID, and aborts and deletes its `.part` file if the producer exits before `finish/1`. |\n| Preview encoder pipeline | Private to `MedEx.Capture` (`Membrane.Opus.Encoder`, `application: :audio`) | Isolated via trapped exits; if the encoder exits, capture notifies the subscriber with `{:med_ex_preview_failed, pid, reason}` and keeps recording. |\n| `MedEx.Preview` peer | Host signaling channel process | A second subscriber displaces the first with an explicit replacement event. Capture continues across peer loss. |\n| `MedEx.Evidence` | Returned to host on `finish/1` | Carries `kind: :audio_pcm16_wav`, content-addressed `artifact_key`, separate `file_sha256` and `pcm_sha256`, sample bounds, and continuity verdict. |","ref":"architecture_and_roadmap.html#process-ownership-and-failure-domains"},{"type":"extras","title":"Releases and roadmap - Architecture and roadmap","doc":"| Capability | Status | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Indexed mono 48 kHz PCM16LE capture → immutable WAV + `MedEx.Evidence` | **Shipped (0.1.0)** | `MedEx.Capture`, `MedEx.Evidence`, 30-minute cap, strict contiguity enforcement. |\n| Bounded live Opus encoding + replaceable send-only WebRTC preview | **Shipped (0.1.0)** | `MedEx.Preview` (`ExWebRTC` + `ExRTP`), host-configurable `:ice_servers`, private `Membrane.Opus.Encoder`. |\n| Browser AudioWorklet PCM capture & LiveView preview hook assets | **Shipped (0.1.0)** | `MedEx.Web.asset_path/1` (`session_hook.js`, `pcm_capture.js`, `pcm_worklet.js`). |\n| Selectable browser input, observed settings, bounded acknowledgement window, producer checks, and relay-only policy | **0.2.0 source** | Host configures acquisition provenance and supplies ICE credentials for browser and server. |\n| Hardware / gateway PCM sources (USB stethoscopes, BLE gateways) | **Planned** | Feed the same `MedEx.Capture.push/3` indexed PCM contract once a named device is verified end-to-end. |\n| Non-audio modalities (multi-channel ECG/PPG waveforms, video tracks) | **Planned** | Will define modality-specific capture and evidence contracts alongside `kind: :audio_pcm16_wav` rather than overloading PCM audio fields. |\n| Out-of-band signal analysis & inference workers (NeuroKit2, WFDB-Python, ONNX, voice AI) | **Planned** | Separately installed/deployed packages or workers consuming finalized `MedEx.Evidence` outside capture and emitting derived results with source digest and algorithm provenance. |\n| Multiparty SFU topologies (e.g. LiveKit) & managed TURN deployments | **Planned** | External media services integrated when a product topology requires multiparty forwarding or NAT relay. |\n\nSee [Host integration](host_integration.md) for the current SDK contract.","ref":"architecture_and_roadmap.html#releases-and-roadmap"},{"type":"extras","title":"Host integration","doc":"# Host integration\n\nThis guide covers everything a Phoenix or Elixir host needs to capture indexed\nmono PCM16LE audio with `MedEx.Capture`, stream an independent live Opus preview\nover `MedEx.Preview`, and serve MedEx's packaged browser helpers.","ref":"host_integration.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Prerequisites - Host integration","doc":"- Elixir `~> 1.20` (tested on Elixir `1.20.5` / OTP `29.1.2`).\n- Ubuntu 26.04 native build packages for WebRTC (`ex_dtls`, `ex_libsrtp`):\n  `build-essential`, `pkg-config`, and `libssl-dev`.\n- Live Opus encoding uses `membrane_opus_plugin`, which uses precompiled\n  `libopus` binaries on supported Linux/macOS targets (install `libopus-dev` if\n  compiling `libopus` from source).\n- Browser microphone capture (`getUserMedia` + `AudioWorklet`) requires a secure\n  context (`https://`, or `http://localhost` / `http://127.0.0.1` for local dev).","ref":"host_integration.html#prerequisites"},{"type":"extras","title":"1. Serve the packaged browser assets - Host integration","doc":"`MedEx.Web.asset_path/1` resolves the three JavaScript files shipped inside\n`:med_ex`:\n\n- `\"session_hook.js\"` — LiveView hook helper (`createMedExHook/1`) for the\n  clinician's receive-only WebRTC preview.\n- `\"pcm_capture.js\"` — patient-browser capture helper (`startPCM`).\n- `\"pcm_worklet.js\"` — `AudioWorkletProcessor` (`\"med-ex-indexed-pcm\"`) loaded\n  by `startPCM`.\n\nServe all three as `application/javascript` from your endpoint:\n\n```elixir\ndefp serve_med_ex_assets(%Plug.Conn{path_info: [\"med_ex\", name]} = conn, _opts)\n     when name in ~w(session_hook.js pcm_capture.js pcm_worklet.js) do\n  conn\n  |> Plug.Conn.put_resp_content_type(\"application/javascript\")\n  |> Plug.Conn.send_file(200, MedEx.Web.asset_path(name))\n  |> Plug.Conn.halt()\nend\n\ndefp serve_med_ex_assets(conn, _opts), do: conn\n```","ref":"host_integration.html#1-serve-the-packaged-browser-assets"},{"type":"extras","title":"2. Supervise live capture in your host - Host integration","doc":"Start a host-owned `DynamicSupervisor` (and optionally a `Registry` if preview\nchannels need to look up active captures by encounter). MedEx starts no global\ncapture processes.\n\n```elixir\n# In your application supervision tree:\nchildren = [\n  {Registry, keys: :unique, name: MyApp.ActiveCapture},\n  {DynamicSupervisor, strategy: :one_for_one, name: MyApp.Captures}\n]\n```\n\nFor the preview example below, start `{Phoenix.PubSub, name: MyApp.PubSub}`\nin the host supervisor as well. Register the encounter in `MyApp.ActiveCapture`\nfrom the producer process and broadcast after the capture starts.\n\nBefore capture, reserve an acquisition ID with its producer and encounter in the\nhost store. Create the attempt's artifact directory and give the browser the ID.\nThis lets the host correlate a finalized WAV with its reservation even if the\nsocket exits during finish. Use the ID for subsequent outcome lookup.\n\nEach capture process takes `:owner`, `:acquisition_id`, and `:artifact_dir`.\n\n```elixir\n{:ok, _} = Registry.register(MyApp.ActiveCapture, encounter_id, nil)\n\n{:ok, capture} =\n  DynamicSupervisor.start_child(\n    MyApp.Captures,\n    {MedEx.Capture,\n     owner: self(),\n     acquisition_id: acquisition_id,\n     artifact_dir: artifact_dir}\n  )\n\nRegistry.update_value(MyApp.ActiveCapture, encounter_id, fn _ -> capture end)\nPhoenix.PubSub.broadcast(MyApp.PubSub, \"preview:\" <> encounter_id, {:capture_started, capture})\n```\n\n`MedEx.Capture` monitors `:owner` and aborts (deleting its temporary `.part`\nfile) if `:owner` exits before `finish/1`. The same PID must call `push/3`\nand `finish/1`. A different caller receives `{:error, :not_owner}` and the\nactive recording continues.","ref":"host_integration.html#2-supervise-live-capture-in-your-host"},{"type":"extras","title":"Handling binary PCM WebSocket frames - Host integration","doc":"In your authenticated WebSocket handler (e.g. a `WebSock` module), decode each\nbinary frame as an 8-byte unsigned big-endian starting sample index followed by\nPCM16LE bytes, push to `MedEx.Capture.push/3`, and reply with text `\"ack\"`:\n\n```elixir\ndef handle_in({< >, [opcode: :binary]}, state) do\n  case MedEx.Capture.push(state.capture, index, pcm) do\n    :ok -> {:push, {:text, \"ack\"}, state}\n    {:error, _reason} -> {:stop, :normal, 1008, {:text, \"invalid_capture\"}, state}\n  end\nend\n\ndef handle_in({\"finish\", [opcode: :text]}, state) do\n  case MedEx.Capture.finish(state.capture) do\n    {:ok, %MedEx.Evidence{} = evidence} ->\n      # Persist finalized evidence before closing the socket.\n      :ok = MyApp.ClinicalStore.mark_ready(state.acquisition_id, evidence)\n      {:stop, :normal, 1000, {:text, \"ready\"}, state}\n\n    {:error, _reason} ->\n      {:stop, :normal, 1011, {:text, \"capture_failed\"}, state}\n  end\nend\n```","ref":"host_integration.html#handling-binary-pcm-websocket-frames"},{"type":"extras","title":"Capture rules and error returns - Host integration","doc":"| Rule / Operation | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| Sample format | Mono 48 kHz signed 16-bit little-endian PCM (`PCM16LE`). |\n| Frame size | Even byte count in `2..1920` (up to 960 samples / 20 ms). Only one short tail frame (`< 1920` bytes) is allowed, immediately before `finish/1`. |\n| Contiguity & limit | `first_sample` must start at `0` and advance contiguously without gaps, up to 30 minutes (`86_400_000` samples). Violations return `{:error, :invalid_frame}` and stop the capture. |\n| `finish/1` | Returns `{:ok, %MedEx.Evidence{}}`, `{:error, :empty_capture}` (0 samples pushed), `{:error, :artifact_conflict}` (existing file digest mismatch), or `{:error, posix}`. |\n| Preview fan-out | Only full 1,920-byte frames are offered to an encoder with demand. A slow subscriber drops preview frames. Starting the first encoder runs in the capture subscription callback. Include this interval when measuring acknowledgement delay under load. |\n\n### `MedEx.Evidence` fields\n\n`MedEx.Capture.finish/1` returns `%MedEx.Evidence{}`:\n\n| Field | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| `:acquisition_id` | Host-provided acquisition ID string |\n| `:artifact_key` | Content-addressed filename (`\" .wav\"`) |\n| `:file_sha256` | Lowercase hex SHA-256 of the complete WAV file |\n| `:pcm_sha256` | Lowercase hex SHA-256 of the raw PCM16LE bytes |\n| `:kind` | `:audio_pcm16_wav` |\n| `:sample_rate_hz` | `48_000` |\n| `:first_sample` | `0` (inclusive) |\n| `:end_sample` | Exclusive ending sample index |\n| `:sample_count` | Total captured mono samples |\n| `:continuity` | `:observed_continuous` |","ref":"host_integration.html#capture-rules-and-error-returns"},{"type":"extras","title":"3. Wire the preview signaling channel - Host integration","doc":"The clinician's Phoenix Channel owns one replaceable `MedEx.Preview` peer.\n`MedEx.Preview.answer/2` sends `{:ex_webrtc, peer.pid, {:connection_state_change, state}}`\nmessages to the channel process. Once `:connected`, subscribe the channel to\nthe active `MedEx.Capture` (only one subscriber is active at a time; a newer\nsubscriber replaces the previous one).\n\n```elixir\ndefmodule MyAppWeb.PreviewChannel do\n  use Phoenix.Channel\n\n  alias MedEx.{Capture, Preview}\n\n  @impl true\n  def join(\"signaling:\" <> encounter_id, %{\"connection_id\" => id}, socket)\n      when is_binary(id) do\n    # Authorize socket.assigns here before allowing join.\n    {:ok, %{session_id: encounter_id},\n     assign(socket,\n       encounter_id: encounter_id,\n       peer: nil,\n       capture: nil,\n       sequence: 0,\n       clock: nil,\n       connected: false\n     )}\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_in(\"offer\", %{\"sdp\" => sdp}, %{assigns: %{peer: nil}} = socket) do\n    opts = MyApp.Media.preview_ice_options(socket.assigns.encounter_id)\n\n    case Preview.answer(sdp, opts) do\n      {:ok, peer, answer_sdp} ->\n        {:reply, {:ok, %{sdp: answer_sdp}}, assign(socket, :peer, peer)}\n\n      {:error, _reason} ->\n        {:reply, {:error, %{reason: \"negotiation_failed\"}}, socket}\n    end\n  end\n\n  @impl true\n  def handle_info(\n        {:ex_webrtc, pid, {:connection_state_change, :connected}},\n        %{assigns: %{peer: %{pid: pid}, connected: false}} = socket\n      ) do\n    encounter_id = socket.assigns.encounter_id\n    :ok = Phoenix.PubSub.subscribe(MyApp.PubSub, \"preview:\" <> encounter_id)\n\n    case Registry.lookup(MyApp.ActiveCapture, encounter_id) do\n      [{_producer, capture}] when is_pid(capture) -> send(self(), {:capture_started, capture})\n      _ -> :ok\n    end\n    {:noreply, assign(socket, :connected, true)}\n  end\n\n  def handle_info({:capture_started, capture}, %{assigns: %{connected: true}} = socket) do\n    case Capture.subscribe(capture) do\n      :ok ->\n        {:noreply, assign(socket, :capture, capture)}\n\n      {:error, :preview_unavailable} ->\n        push(socket, \"preview_failed\", %{})\n        {:noreply, socket}\n    end\n  catch\n    :exit, _ -> {:noreply, socket}\n  end\n\n  def handle_info(\n        {:med_ex_preview, capture, sample_index, packet},\n        %{assigns: %{capture: capture, peer: peer, sequence: seq, clock: clock}} = socket\n      ) do\n    tick = next_tick(clock, capture, sample_index)\n    :ok = Preview.send_opus(peer, packet, seq, tick)\n    :ok = Capture.demand(capture)\n    {:noreply, assign(socket, sequence: seq + 1, clock: {capture, sample_index, tick})}\n  end\n\n  def handle_info({:med_ex_preview_replaced, capture}, %{assigns: %{capture: capture}} = socket) do\n    push(socket, \"preview_replaced\", %{})\n    {:noreply, assign(socket, capture: nil, connected: false)}\n  end\n\n  def handle_info({:med_ex_preview_failed, capture, _reason}, %{assigns: %{capture: capture}} = socket) do\n    push(socket, \"preview_failed\", %{})\n    {:noreply, assign(socket, :capture, nil)}\n  end\n\n  def handle_info(\n        {:ex_webrtc, pid, {:connection_state_change, state}},\n        %{assigns: %{peer: %{pid: pid}}} = socket\n      )\n      when state in [:failed, :closed],\n      do: {:stop, :normal, socket}\n\n  def handle_info(_msg, socket), do: {:noreply, socket}\n\n  @impl true\n  def terminate(_reason, socket) do\n    if peer = socket.assigns[:peer], do: Preview.close(peer)\n    :ok\n  end\n\n  # Keep RTP media timestamps monotonic if a new capture starts on the same peer.\n  defp next_tick(nil, _capture, index), do: index\n  defp next_tick({capture, last, tick}, capture, index), do: tick + index - last\n  defp next_tick({_prev, _last, tick}, _capture, _index), do: tick + 960\nend\n```\n\nFor the example, implement `MyApp.Media.preview_ice_options/1` to return\n`[ice_servers: servers, ice_transport_policy: :all]` or use `:relay` with TURN\ncredentials scoped to the preview peer. Give the conversation peers and browser\npreview the corresponding WebRTC `iceServers` and `iceTransportPolicy`\nconfiguration with credentials scoped to their sessions. Defaults are an empty\nserver list and `:all`. A relay deployment can inspect each selected candidate\npair with browser `getStats()`. Measure PCM acknowledgement delay separately on\nthe authenticated WebSocket.","ref":"host_integration.html#3-wire-the-preview-signaling-channel"},{"type":"extras","title":"4. Browser preview hook (session_hook.js) - Host integration","doc":"Wrap the clinician preview controls in a LiveView container with\n**`phx-update=\"ignore\"`** (required so LiveView DOM diffs do not tear down the\nactive ` ` stream), `data-token` (sent in Phoenix Socket params), an\n` ` element, and an optional `[role=\"status\"]` element:\n\n```heex\n \n   Play preview \n   Disconnect \n   Reconnect \n    \n   idle \n \n```\n\nRegister the hook on your `LiveSocket`:\n\n```js\nimport { Socket } from \"/assets/phoenix.mjs\";\nimport { LiveSocket } from \"/assets/phoenix_live_view.esm.js\";\nimport { createMedExHook } from \"/med_ex/session_hook.js\";\n\nconst csrfToken = document.querySelector('meta[name=\"csrf-token\"]').content;\nconst liveSocket = new LiveSocket(\"/live\", Socket, {\n  params: { _csrf_token: csrfToken },\n  hooks: {\n    MedExSessionHook: createMedExHook({\n      Socket,\n      socketPath: \"/socket\",\n      topic: el => \"signaling:\" + el.dataset.encounterId,\n      play: \"#preview-play\",\n      disconnect: \"#preview-disconnect\",\n      reconnect: \"#preview-reconnect\",\n      rtcConfig: async el => {\n        const response = await fetch(\"/encounters/\" + encodeURIComponent(el.dataset.encounterId) + \"/ice\");\n        if (!response.ok) throw new Error(\"ICE configuration unavailable\");\n        return response.json(); // {iceServers, iceTransportPolicy}\n      }\n    })\n  }\n});\nliveSocket.connect();\n```\n\nChannel protocol expected by `createMedExHook`:\n\n1. Joins `topic(el)` with `{ connection_id: crypto.randomUUID() }`, expecting\n   `{ session_id }`.\n2. Gathers browser ICE candidates and pushes `\"offer\"` with `{ sdp }`, expecting\n   `{ sdp }` answer.\n3. Handles `\"preview_failed\"` and `\"preview_replaced\"` by closing the peer and\n   displaying the appropriate status. The clinician can select Reconnect.\n   The hook evaluates `rtcConfig(el)` for each new connection. A host with\n   static configuration can pass `iceServers` and `iceTransportPolicy` directly.","ref":"host_integration.html#4-browser-preview-hook-session_hook-js"},{"type":"extras","title":"5. Browser live PCM capture (pcm_capture.js & pcm_worklet.js) - Host integration","doc":"Call `startPCM` from a user gesture, such as clicking Start. Provide separate\nbuttons with IDs `finish-capture` and `abort-capture`. Enable Finish from the\nrecording callback once the server acknowledges the first frame.\n\n```js\nimport { startPCM } from \"/med_ex/pcm_capture.js\";\n\n// Host helper opens the authenticated socket and reads the acquisition ID.\nconst {socket, acquisitionId} = await reserveCapture();\nconst handle = await startPCM(\n  socket,\n  \"/med_ex/pcm_worklet.js\",\n  (outcome, measurements) => showCaptureOutcome(acquisitionId, outcome, measurements),\n  () => enableFinish(),\n  {\n    deviceId: diagnosticInput.value,\n    onSource: settings => saveLogicalSource(acquisitionId, settings)\n  }\n);\n\n// Use separate buttons for the two terminal actions.\ndocument.querySelector(\"#finish-capture\").onclick = () => handle.finish();\ndocument.querySelector(\"#abort-capture\").onclick = () => handle.abort();\n```","ref":"host_integration.html#5-browser-live-pcm-capture-pcm_capture-js-pcm_worklet-js"},{"type":"extras","title":"Source and timing - Host integration","doc":"Offer the browser's `audioinput` devices for separate conversation and\ndiagnostic input selections. An empty diagnostic selection requests the default\nmicrophone. A selected `deviceId` becomes an exact constraint. The helper asks\nfor mono with echo cancellation, noise suppression and auto gain disabled.\nIt calls `onSource` with the track's `getSettings()` fields, its `label`, and\n`contextSampleRate`. The callback may return a promise. PCM begins only after\nthe promise resolves. Unsupported settings are absent. Device IDs identify\nlogical inputs in the browser's origin. Obtain hardware identity or calibration\nseparately if relevant.\n\nThe audio context runs at 48 kHz. Track `sampleRate` describes the source as\nreported by the browser and can differ from `contextSampleRate`. The host can\ntimestamp the arrival of the first accepted PCM frame and derive duration in\nseconds as `sample_count / 48_000`. Store that timing basis and the actor with\nthe attempt. The continuity verdict covers consecutive browser render samples\nfrom the first emitted frame.","ref":"host_integration.html#source-and-timing"},{"type":"extras","title":"Live PCM wire protocol and outcome codes - Host integration","doc":"Each binary frame has an 8-byte unsigned big-endian `first_sample` index and\nup to 960 mono PCM16LE samples. Send exactly one ordered text `\"ack\"` after\neach successful writer call. The first acknowledgement triggers `onRecording()`.\nFile synchronization and installation happen at finish.\n\nThe delay budget is **250 ms sustained plus 50 ms jitter**. At 20 ms per full\nframe this gives 15 frames, plus one for scheduling at the boundary. A frame\ntakes one of the 16 slots when it is posted from the worklet. The slot stays\noccupied through the main-thread queue, WebSocket send queue, and writer until\nits acknowledgement reaches the worklet. Another frame can be assembled while\nall slots are occupied. The maximum logical buffered wire data, including\n8-byte frame headers, is **17 × 1,928 = 32,776 bytes**. This bounds application\naudio, independent of browser/OS transport overhead. If a completed frame\ncannot be sent, the worklet reports `capture_overflow` and capture closes.\n\n`handle.finish()` sends the short tail, if present, followed by text\n`\"finish\"`. The host replies with a terminal outcome after committing the\nrecording. `onOutcome(outcome, measurements)` receives `peakBufferedBytes`\n(the worklet high-water mark, reported on each frame and worklet termination)\nand `maxAckDelayMs` (longest observed interval from WebSocket send to the\ncorresponding reply, including page scheduling). Premature socket closure\nreturns the latest reported measurements. On a lost final reply the host can\nretrieve the outcome using the acquisition ID.\n\n| Outcome | Meaning |\n| --- | --- |\n| Host text frame (e.g. `\"ready\"`, `\"capture_failed\"`, `\"invalid_capture\"`) | Terminal response from the host. |\n| `\"setup_failed\"` | Permission, input constraints, source callback, 48 kHz context, worklet or socket setup failed. `startPCM` also rejects. |\n| `\"capture_source_timeout\"` | A contiguous full frame could not be established within one second of startup. |\n| `\"capture_gap\"` | Missing input or a skipped render index after the first full frame. |\n| `\"capture_overflow\"` | A frame was ready while all 16 slots awaited writer acknowledgements. |\n| `\"invalid_ack\"` | An acknowledgement arrived with no outstanding PCM frame. |\n| `\"source_ended\"` | Browser media track ended unexpectedly. |\n| `\"disconnected\"` | WebSocket closed or errored before a terminal host outcome arrived. |\n| `\"aborted\"` | Host browser code called `handle.abort()`. |","ref":"host_integration.html#live-pcm-wire-protocol-and-outcome-codes"},{"type":"extras","title":"Source development","doc":"# Source development\n\nThese instructions apply to the source repository checkout at\n . They are not needed when installing\n`:med_ex` as a Hex dependency.","ref":"source_development.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"Repository layout - Source development","doc":"| Path | Role |\n| --- | --- |\n| `core/med_rtc` | `MedEx.Capture`, `MedEx.Evidence`, `MedEx.Preview`, WAV writer, and private Membrane Opus encoder. |\n| `core/med_web` | `MedEx.Web` asset locator and browser JS (`session_hook.js`, `pcm_capture.js`, `pcm_worklet.js`). |\n| `build_support/weld.exs` | Weld manifest projecting `core/med_rtc` and `core/med_web` into the single `:med_ex` Hex package. |\n| `dist/release_bundles/` | Gitignored output directory where `mix weld.release.prepare` writes the generated `project/`, rendered `docs/`, and `.tar` archive. |","ref":"source_development.html#repository-layout"},{"type":"extras","title":"Prerequisites (Ubuntu 26.04) - Source development","doc":"Install system packages:\n\n```sh\nsudo apt-get install -y git curl tar build-essential pkg-config libssl-dev\n```\n\n*(Install `libopus-dev` as well if compiling `membrane_opus_plugin` from source\ninstead of using precompiled binaries.)*\n\nActivate the exact Erlang and Elixir versions pinned in `.tool-versions`\n(`erlang 29.1.2`, `elixir 1.20.5-otp-29`) via `asdf` or `mise`.","ref":"source_development.html#prerequisites-ubuntu-26-04"},{"type":"extras","title":"Build, test, and prepare a release bundle - Source development","doc":"```sh\n./onboard.sh\nmix ci\nnode --test core/med_web/test/*.mjs\nmix weld.release.prepare\n```\n\n`mix weld.release.prepare` prints the path to the generated bundle under\n`dist/release_bundles/med_ex/ - /`, containing:\n\n- `project/` — standalone generated `:med_ex` Mix project (can be referenced as\n  a local path dependency before Hex publication, or tested directly via\n  `mix deps.get && mix test`).\n- `docs/` — rendered ExDoc HTML preview (`docs/index.html`).\n- `med_ex- .tar` — exact Hex archive.\n- `release.json` — source revision, verification checks, and SHA-256 digests.","ref":"source_development.html#build-test-and-prepare-a-release-bundle"},{"type":"extras","title":"Changelog","doc":"# Changelog","ref":"changelog.html"},{"type":"extras","title":"0.2.0 (unreleased) - Changelog","doc":"- Authorize capture writes and finish by producer PID. Notify a displaced preview listener.\n- Select a logical diagnostic input and expose actual browser settings before streaming.\n- Budget 250 ms of PCM acknowledgement delay plus 50 ms of jitter and report transport measurements.\n- Apply host-selected relay policy and ICE servers to browser and server preview.","ref":"changelog.html#0-2-0-unreleased"},{"type":"extras","title":"0.1.0 - Changelog","doc":"- Record indexed browser PCM as content-addressed WAV evidence.\n- Encode live Opus on a bounded preview branch with replaceable WebRTC peers.\n- Provide host-configurable ICE, browser capture assets, and standalone integration guides.","ref":"changelog.html#0-1-0"},{"type":"extras","title":"License","doc":"MIT License\n\nCopyright (c) 2026 nshkrdotcom\n\nPermission is hereby granted, free of charge, to any person obtaining a copy\nof this software and associated documentation files (the \"Software\"), to deal\nin the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights\nto use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and/or sell\ncopies of the Software, and to permit persons to whom the Software is\nfurnished to do so, subject to the following conditions:\n\nThe above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in all\ncopies or substantial portions of the Software.\n\nTHE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED \"AS IS\", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR\nIMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY,\nFITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE AND NONINFRINGEMENT. IN NO EVENT SHALL THE\nAUTHORS OR COPYRIGHT HOLDERS BE LIABLE FOR ANY CLAIM, DAMAGES OR OTHER\nLIABILITY, WHETHER IN AN ACTION OF CONTRACT, TORT OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM,\nOUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH THE SOFTWARE OR THE USE OR OTHER DEALINGS IN THE\nSOFTWARE.","ref":"license.html"}],"proglang":"elixir","content_type":"text/markdown","producer":{"name":"ex_doc","version":"0.40.5"}}